    "narrative": "The core of the Austin Waves attack tonight rests squarely on the shoulders of **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 83.29 efficiency score makes him the premier play in our lineup. Facing Yesavage, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a high-upside matchup against a starter with a 4.57 xERA, allowing his premium batted-ball profile and batting order advantage at #3 to maximize his run-production ceiling. While **Coby Mayo** also draws the same favorable assignment against Yesavage, his score of 62.86 is slightly suppressed by a dynamic platoon disadvantage despite his prime #4 spot in the order. Both players are positioned to exploit the park factors currently favoring hitters, providing a high floor for our counting stats.\n\nThe optimization process was straightforward today given the heavy rotation of players currently sidelined. With **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Andy Pages** all unavailable due to rest or IL stints, our depth is being severely tested. **Jacob Wilson**, **Nasim Nunez**, and **Heliot Ramos** remain the primary candidates to fill the gaps, though none achieved the necessary score to force a change in our primary construction. **Jordan Westburg** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** continue to hover near the fringe of the starting rotation, but their recent plate discipline metrics were not enough to displace the current middle-infield starters. \n\nMoving forward, the primary risk remains the scarcity of stolen bases; with **Nasim Nunez** and **Brayan Rocchio** failing to provide high-ceiling output lately, we are essentially banking on **Gunnar Henderson** to anchor the entire team's speed production. We are closely monitoring the status of **Miguel Vargas**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Josh Jung** to see if their platoon splits improve against mid-week pitching rotations. For today, maintain strict adherence to the game cap management strategy\u2014unless a specific player\u2019s efficiency spikes above 70, we will keep **Drake Baldwin**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Tommy White** on the bench to preserve our flexibility for the season's final push.",
